[Catch2 PATCH] Add vstest reporter (.trx XML output)

Add a new bundled reporter that emits Visual Studio Test (.trx) format,
suitable for ingestion by Azure DevOps Pipelines and similar test-result
consumers that prefer the VS Test schema.

The reporter is built on the v3 streaming reporter model:
StreamingReporterBase + native testCasePartialStarting/Ended callbacks
provide per-traversal granularity. Per-traversal stdout/stderr content
is sliced from the process-wide OutputRedirectSinks (see the framework
redirect machinery) via position-based getLatestContents() reads at each
section traversal's completion. The .trx XML is emitted incrementally
between test-case traversals when output is to a file (reopen-and-
truncate between emissions for crash recovery), or once at testRunEnded
when output is to stdout/console.

The reporter takes ownership of the framework's process-wide sinks at
construction time via IncrementalSectionTraversal::setRedirectSinksFromConfig.
Sink ownership is transferred from one traversal to the next via
setRedirectSinksFromPredecessor as test traversals complete.
testCaseEnded captures any residual TestCaseStats stdout/stderr (the
sum delivered when no process-wide sinks are active and the per-test
OutputRedirect was used instead).

Custom options are read from the reporter spec's customOptions map:
  Xsource-path-prefix       common path prefix to strip from source
                            file references in error messages
  Xreport-attachment-paths  semicolon-delimited paths to attach to
                            <ResultSummary>/<ResultFiles>

